/target
/captures
# A SAVED PLAN IS A SECRET. `terraform plan -out=<f>` writes a zip carrying `tfplan`,
# `tfstate` AND `tfstate-prev` — i.e. the full production state, including the argon2
# `admin_password_hash` in cleartext. Treat a plan file exactly like a tfvars file.
#
# The filename is CHOSEN BY THE OPERATOR, so these globs are a backstop, not the
# guarantee — they can only cover spellings someone thought of. Both extensions are
# listed because the repo's own docs used the one the ignore list missed: every
# documented invocation said `-out=tf.plan` while only `*.tfplan` was ignored (fixed
# in the same commit as this comment). Keep the docs and these globs in agreement,
# and prefer writing plans OUTSIDE the worktree entirely.
terraform/.terraform/
terraform/backend.hcl
terraform/artifacts/
terraform/*.tfplan
terraform/*.plan
terraform/*.tfvars
# The `-out=<f>` glob only catches files ENDING `.tfplan`/`.plan`. A JSON/text
# EXPORT of a plan (`terraform show -json … > plan.json`) carries the same
# cleartext secrets and matches none of the above. Added 2026-09-07 after a
# `git add -A` beside a fresh `plan.json` (AWS keys inside) was stopped by
# GitHub push protection — the backstop below is so the next one never reaches
# the wire in the first place. `tfplan*` catches bare `tfplan`/`tfplan.bin` too.
terraform/plan.json
terraform/plan.txt
terraform/tfplan*
terraform-iam/.terraform/
terraform-iam/backend.hcl
terraform-iam/*.tfplan
terraform-iam/*.plan
terraform-iam/*.tfvars
terraform-iam/plan.json
terraform-iam/plan.txt
terraform-iam/tfplan*

# impeccable ephemeral state is ignored by .impeccable/.gitignore (live/sessions/,
# live/annotations/, live/server.json); design.json + live/config.json are tracked
# source (the design hook reads them). A root-level .impeccable/ rule here would be
# a no-op-vs-tracked-files contradiction (#80 finding 3).
.worktrees/
